{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00400 - MONDO_1461",
  "verbalization": "Griseofulvin, a fungal antifungal agent, is implicated in the treatment of Tinea Corporis through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Griseofulvin may be repurposed for Tinea Corporis, as it is associated with Tinea Unguium and Tinea Barbae, both of which are fungal infections. These conditions are similarly treated with Miconazole, Ciclopirox, and Tolnaftate, which are also antifungal agents. The shared indication for Tinea Corporis across these pathways indicates a potential mechanistic link, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role of Griseofulvin in the treatment of Tinea Corporis through antifungal activity, though further research is needed to confirm this relationship and understand the underlying biological processes.",
